<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-MIDI LIBRE FOURTH STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-MIDI LIBRE FOURTH STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>MONTPELLIER, France 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in</p>
<p>the 145.5-km fourth stage of the Midi Libre cycling race from</p>
<p>Ales to Montpellier on Friday:</p>
<p>Stage placings:</p>
<p>1. Gordon Frazer (Canada) Mutuelle Seine et Marne  3 hours 15</p>
<p>minutes 49 seconds</p>
<p>2. Frederic Moncassin (France) GAN</p>
<p>3. Adriano Baffi (Italy) US Postal Service</p>
<p>4. Pascal Chanteur (France) Casino</p>
<p>5. Arvis Piziks (Estonia) Rabobank</p>
<p>6. Andrei Teteriuk (Khazakstan) Lotto</p>
<p>7. Rolf Aldag (German) Telekom</p>
<p>8. Christophe Mengin (France) Francaise des Jeux</p>
<p>9. Thierry Gouvenou (France) Bigmat Auber 93</p>
<p> 10. Sergei Ivanov (Russia) TVM	 all same time</p>
<p>Overall standings:</p>
<p> 1. Alberto Elli (Italy) Casino   18 hours 29 minuts 3 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Laurent Dufaux (Sitzerland) Festina    8:14 minutes behind</p>
<p> 3. Bart Voskamp (Netherlands) TVM	   8:17</p>
<p> 4. George Totschnig (Germany) Telekom     8:18</p>
<p> 5. Arturas Kasputis (Lituania) Casino     8:26</p>
<p> 6. David Plaza (France) Cofidis	     same time</p>
<p> 7. Bo Hamburger (Denmark) TVM		 11:52</p>
<p> 8. Angel Casero Moreno (Spain) Banesto    12:24</p>
<p> 9. Laurent Desbiens (France) Cofidis	18:26</p>
<p> 10. Luca Gelfi (Italy) Brescialat	   18:39</p>
</text>
